  "body": "#2001 has merged; this PR is based on main.\n\n## What changed\n\nShow the selected tool's editable settings directly in Properties.\nUse the same form from the browser and the setup's Tool list.\nKeep geometry, holder/body/profile, cutting data, tool numbers and identification fields with the selected tool.\nMove catalog browsing, Add/New, import/export and import options into a separate Tool library dock tab.\nOpen that tab from Tools or browser View > Tool library… without replacing the Properties subject.\nKeep new-tool creation in its existing window.\nPreserve the explicit editor's original wide layout and command paths.\nName per-tool metadata Tool information to distinguish it from library browsing.\n\nThe control split and alternatives are recorded in docs/decisions/2002-tool-properties.md.\nSource inspection found no control literally named Support features and no MCP or script verb that opens the catalog by page name.\nParent head: 028a0ad0ed6711e39fc584d55be8a987906a81c5.\nEffort: medium.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Before: tool selection shows the catalog in Properties](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d006690894ca70318e29a6904a02e109891fe949/2002/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![After: tool selection shows editable settings in Properties](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d006690894ca70318e29a6904a02e109891fe949/2002/after.png)\n\nCatalog:\n\n![Tool library in its own dock tab](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/d006690894ca70318e29a6904a02e109891fe949/2002/catalog.png)\n\n## Cause\n\nTool selection opened a combined summary and library page.\nThe editable form lived in a separate window.\nThe Tools action also replaced the Properties target with that library page.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe core navigation pins failed at runtime before the fix.\nThe setup-list pin failed before its routing change.\nAll five new structural pins pass:\n\n- selected_tool_settings_live_in_properties_without_the_catalog\n- tools_ribbon_opens_a_docked_catalog_without_retargeting_properties\n- setup_tool_list_edit_opens_tool_settings_in_properties\n- browser_library_door_and_tool_selection_focus_their_own_dock_tabs\n- properties_tool_apply_and_undo_use_the_command_history\n\nThe Apply pin uses a real pointer drag and click.\nIt checks that staging leaves the world unchanged, Apply changes it, and Undo restores it.\nAccessKit labels and roles pin the settings and catalog surfaces.\nExisting explicit-editor tests also require exactly one Diameter field surface.\n\nSix mutations failed at runtime and passed after restoration:\n\n- Restore upstream/main pages.rs: red/green.\n- Restore upstream/main actions.rs: red/green.\n- Restore upstream/main tool_list_page.rs: red/green.\n- Remove dock-tab focus: red/green.\n- Remove browser-selection editor closure: red/green.\n- Remove Properties field suppression while the explicit editor is open: red/green.\n\ncargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main: green, four steps, zero failures.\nThe final application group passed 257 test binaries.\nThe final UI unit suite passed 821 tests with six existing ignored tests.\ncargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings: green.\nThe wide editor retains its original horizontal allocation and fixed widths so body controls remain reachable.\nNo body pointer test was weakened.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\ngit diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" is empty.\nNo snapshot PNG changed.\nReview screenshots live only on the fork's images-only pr-screenshots branch.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNative OS window interaction and release pixel snapshots were not run.\nReview images render the shipping shell under egui_kittest with its viewport fixture.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2001 changes tool_editor_window and is the stack parent.\nThis branch preserves its waterjet editor behavior.\n\n- #1931 and #1717 change WCS Properties and tests: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1999 changes ribbon sizing and shell constants: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1798 adds reporting controls: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1996 changes shell structural assertions: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2000 changes document camera framing: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1938 adds contour start/exit controls and module declarations: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1753 changes machine tooltip expectations: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1685 adds stock-fit test registration: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1687 changes browser file-menu assertions: touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Show selected tool settings in Properties and move library browsing and import/export to a separate docked Tool library panel.\n\nFixes #2002\n\n",
